# Build artefacts and local-only files.
#
# Artefact patterns are anchored to the repository root (`/`) on purpose: an
# unanchored pattern such as `bin/` also matches nested source directories, and
# a broad ignore rule is how a source file (in particular the process
# entrypoint) silently drops out of a commit without anyone noticing.
/bin/
/coverage.out
/coverage.html
*.test
# `.env` stays global: a local secrets file must never be committed from any
# directory, not just the repository root.
.env

# `cmd/server/main.go` is the process entrypoint described in
# docs/engineering_guide.md; it is source, never an artefact. Re-include it
# explicitly so a future ignore rule cannot discard it again.
!/cmd/server/main.go
